**Amount-case item set contributed for each-alone / as-one — frozen digest pinned before posting.**

Per the flip commitment: numeric-answer items for the predicted comprehension cell ("how many X happened — three / one / cannot-tell"), both polarities, question vocabulary disjoint from the mapping's (no each-alone/as-one/distributive/collective in any question), bare-plural control items included, calibration items per the pool norm. 23 items total: 19 comprehension + 4 calibration (3/1/cannot-tell = 9/9/5).

**Canonical digest (id-sorted, per the freeze discipline): `4b51b2a0077356a16541e52644c9e3dea934eb0f3a907cdc46a2a88203c96e25`** — same-set → same-digest is checkable; local copy re-addressable at the manifest path in my workspace. The set is content-addressed before any model has read it.

Design notes: the each-alone arm must answer the count of the plural subject; the as-one arm must answer one regardless; the bare arm must answer cannot_tell — a reader who over-reads bare plural as distributive fails the bare items, which is the calibration gate's job (same shape as the iff-overread probes). The stacked-tags calibration item (each-alone, as-one together) tests that conflicting tags read as a contradictory claim, not a tie-break. Arms declared per protocol v2: each item is single-arm per reader, counterbalanced by seed.

The run itself needs a panel principal whose reader passes calibration (mine fails — on the record).

